                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Take On The Gravel In A Mediocre Way[/h1]\nThe return of a legendary off-road racing game! Enjoy an extreme experience while becoming an expert in a demanding simulation. Take on the challenges of rallies, rallycross, drifts, buggies and hill climbs, and set off on a spectacular journey across every continent.\n\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/ATReviews]Follow My Review Group Here![/url]\n\n💾Graphics - V-Rally 4 offers a decent selection of environments and racing locations, but unfortunately, its visuals haven't aged particularly well. While the different locations provide some variety, the overall presentation feels outdated and somewhat bland compared to other racing games at the time. Vehicle models are reasonably detailed, but the environments, lighting, and general visual effects lack the polish needed to make the experience truly stand out. For a game released in 2018, I expected a little more visually, especially considering how much of the experience revolves around driving through different landscapes. There are also some immersion-breaking details that become noticeable during rally events. One particular disappointment is the windshield dirt mechanic, which would be much more enjoyable if the windshield wipers actually cleaned the dirt off effectively. Small details like this could have made the driving experience feel considerably more realistic. \n\n🎮Gameplay - This game has a surprisingly decent amount of gameplay variety, with several different racing disciplines to keep things interesting. Rally, Rallycross, Hillclimb, Buggy, and Extreme-Khana provide different driving experiences, while the vehicle selection offers plenty of options to experiment with. I particularly enjoyed the car tuning and upgrade system, which gives you an incentive to improve your vehicles as you progress. Career mode also has a team management system where you can recruit specialists to help manage different aspects of your operation. It's a nice addition that gives the career progression a little more depth than simply completing races and purchasing new cars. Now unfortunately, the gameplay has several frustrating issues that hold it back. Rally difficulty feels particularly inconsistent, with certain events becoming unnecessarily difficult and making progression more frustrating than rewarding. Career mode also becomes repetitive after a while, as you're constantly cycling through similar events without enough meaningful changes to keep things fresh. Another persistent annoyance is the \"Can't Connect to V-Rally Servers\" message appearing after practically every race, which quickly becomes irritating. Combined with the inconsistent difficulty and repetitive progression, these problems make the overall experience feel much less polished than it could have been. V-Rally 4 has some genuinely enjoyable mechanics, but it struggles to maintain that enjoyment over longer play sessions.\n\n🕛Playtime - The game does offer all cars and tracks right out of the gate to mess with on quick play mode. This does offer some replayability as you can just do simple races for fun. The career mode is a  bit repetitive, so it’s a one and done deal in my opinion. Besides that, this game doesn’t offer too much playtime besides trying to get all of the achievements. \n\n🎧Sound - Sound design is pretty decent. The engine sounds are really good and most, if not all cars do sound unique from each other. I will also say that the engine sound does help make the driving experience feel more engaging. Also the sound of gravel, mud, and tires sliding across different surfaces adds a satisfying layer of immersion. I will say the menu music is horrible and doesn’t really feel like it fits with the game. Besides the music, this game does offer some solid sound design. Not perfect, but pretty good for the time of release.\n\n❗Bugs❗- I haven’t really encountered any bugs in this game, besides some very minor visuals glitches. Besides that, this game did offer a smooth experience. You should have no issues with glitches or bugs.\n\n🔅Performance - Performance was amazing for me. I was playing on max settings, 1600p resolution and I was getting 200+ FPS. This game ran fantastic for me. I also had no crashes or stutters while playing. You should be fine running this game.\n\n✔️Pro’s✔️\n[list]\n[*]Solid sound design\n[*]Car tuning/upgrades\n[*]Really good optimization\n[*]Decent variety of vehicles\n[*]Team management/recruiting for career mode\n[*]Good variety of race modes (including hillclimb)\n[/list]\n\n❌Con’s❌\n[list]\n[*]Rally difficulty feels broken\n[*]Music is terrible and generic\n[*]Visuals look outdated and bland\n[*]Career mode get really repetitive\n[*]Can’t wipe dirt off with functioning wipers\n[*]“Can’t Connect to V-Rally Servers” after every race\n[/list]\n        \n🏆Rating - 5/10\nWait for a big sale 75% off or more.\n\n🔗Conclusion - V-Rally 4 offers a decent experience for Rally fans. I will say though that compared to many other rally games on Steam, it just feels and looks very average. It’s not a horrible game, but it does suffer from some issues. Like the terrible difficulty spikes on Rally events, the repetitive career mode, and bland visuals that have not aged well at all. The game does offer some good variety in races and vehicles, decent team management system, and okay physics (passable at best). If you see this game on a super steep sale, then sure give this a try. Besides that, I’d look somewhere else since Steam does offer a great variety of Rally games.\n\nhttps://store.steampowered.com/app/658700/VRally_4/\n\nLinks to help you in V-Rally 4:\n[olist]\n[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2488797360] \"Rally Fan\" Achievement Exploit Guide [/url]\n[/olist]",
